       "type": "text",
       "html": "<p><strong>Regulation A</strong> (often called \"Reg A+\") is a <strong>mini-registration</strong> for smaller offerings. The issuer files a <strong>Form 1-A offering circular</strong> that the SEC must <em>qualify</em>, instead of a full prospectus. It may also <strong>\"test the waters\"</strong> to gauge interest before committing to the deal.</p>"
